# Repositories
 
The Heighliner organization maintains the following repositories, sorted by type.
 
## Applications
 
Repositories that contain a ready-to-use app product.
 
| Repository | Description |
|------------|--------------|
| [Beacon](https://github.com/Blue-Heighliner/Beacon) | Tracker for equipment and inventory. |
 
## Engines
 
Repositories that contain a near ready-to-use app product, built and distributed as a NuGet package. Another project can use the engine library with overridden interfaces to inject and drive how the app product operates.
 
| Repository | Description |
|------------|--------------|
| [Comlink](https://github.com/Blue-Heighliner/Comlink) | Message client that can be configured for either peer-to-peer or server-client communication. |
 
## Utilities
 
Repositories that contain a useful utility app for development.
 
| Repository | Description |
|------------|--------------|
| [Nuget-Fetcher](https://github.com/Blue-Heighliner/Nuget-Fetcher) | Tool for pulling all nupkg files for all NuGet dependencies from a project's Directory.Packages.props file for offline development/ |
 
## Libraries
 
Repositories that contain a library, built as a NuGet package, for sharing general functionality across other repositories.
 
| Repository | Description |
|------------|--------------|
| [Micro-Gate](https://github.com/Blue-Heighliner/Micro-Gate) | API for interacting with MicroGate SyncLink devices. |
| [Open-Frame-Transport](https://github.com/Blue-Heighliner/Open-Frame-Transport) | Application-layer message protocol that runs on top of TCP and TLS. |
